{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"124ba0377a82aa9d0d8e08191894a566f883c759e503978f1701f0d122d97d99","slug":"processing-steps","location":"/docs/processing-steps.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Processing steps","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Lukas Hörtnagl","given":"Lukas","family":"Hörtnagl"},"name":"Lukas Hörtnagl","email":"lukas.hoertnagl@usys.ethz.ch","affiliations":["ETH Zürich"],"id":"contributors-dev\\manuscripts\\ms-timelag-comparison\\myst-generated-uid-0","corresponding":true}],"affiliations":[{"id":"ETH Zürich","name":"ETH Zürich"}],"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"processing-steps.md","url":"/ms-timelag-comparison/build/processing-steps-9b16d1838aea7add40a2987beb985771.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page describes the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"BxAhaRHE9i"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PWB","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"nNhmT4URwu"}],"key":"t5jwQ2Fvx1"},{"type":"text","value":" time-lag method used to produce the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"TGDRy1xvEt"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*-5","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"BDPaXdFSKC"},{"type":"text","value":"\n","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"pOoNCDTc5h"},{"type":"link","url":"/processing-versions","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"processing versions","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"RDA7szPNia"}],"urlSource":"processing-versions.md","dataUrl":"/processing-versions.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"LwjPlNmFkl"},{"type":"text","value":", and the diive workflow that\napplies it.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"mO94ufFXIw"}],"key":"KtEaUS8SpB"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The PWB time-lag method","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"hGV1KuXs4f"}],"identifier":"the-pwb-time-lag-method","label":"The PWB time-lag method","html_id":"the-pwb-time-lag-method","implicit":true,"key":"KPoSILxIrh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For reactive and trace gases such as N₂O and CH₄, the gas-wind cross-correlation\nis often too weak for conventional covariance-maximization (CM) to pinpoint the\ntime lag reliably. The ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"dWHQuJZClD"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*-5","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"tmkugDYmnq"},{"type":"text","value":" versions instead use the Pre-Whitening with\nBlock-bootstrap (PWB) method (Vitale et al., 2024), as implemented in ","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"KPPgqAXbiH"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diive","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"WxSR8MLenf"},{"type":"text","value":". It\nworks in two stages.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"tbKfRVcNJa"}],"key":"TQkve2Ai4s"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-whitening.","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"cqpCHKKejl"}],"key":"eGP8gNJZSp"},{"type":"text","value":" An AR(","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"P8NxDjRFu9"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"p","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"HVJQU4VBFa"}],"key":"xsplQWuPNH"},{"type":"text","value":") filter (order chosen by AIC) removes serial\nautocorrelation from each series before the cross-correlation function (CCF) is\ncomputed. Turbulent wind and trace-gas series are strongly autocorrelated, which\nbroadens and distorts the CCF peak. Whitening the residuals sharpens the peak and\ngives a cleaner lag estimate.","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"L1cUgY7XVi"}],"key":"n83XDXM36X"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Block-bootstrap.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"ZqzWEpcjJ7"}],"key":"rMAK79e3zM"},{"type":"text","value":" Instead of a single CCF over the whole averaging period, the\nmethod draws ","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"zEyl1u7NfG"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"N","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"rhfOLU6JKU"}],"key":"orfysOViPW"},{"type":"text","value":"ᵦ resampled series by moving-block resampling, where overlapping\nblocks of length ","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"xJGEm39Amt"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"L","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"VvyzLTkEr9"}],"key":"K6w9YEpzwW"},{"type":"text","value":" preserve local autocorrelation. It detects the peak lag in\neach resample and summarizes the resulting distribution by its mode (the lag\nestimate) and a 95% Highest Density Interval (HDI). A narrow HDI means resampling\nconsistently finds the same lag, which is the method’s reliability criterion.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"xJGKuiu26l"}],"key":"wMYhRn8mUX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sonic temperature (T_sonic) is required. Four CCF combinations are evaluated\n(scalar × W and scalar × T_sonic, each with a scalar, W, or T_sonic AR filter),\nand the combination with the strongest peak is selected. The T_sonic-based\ncombinations often recover a cleaner lag for gases with a weak scalar × W signal.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"vhVdcZXttl"}],"key":"lL5jEdlQku"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference: Vitale D. et al. (2024), ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"OPKgOr9DPE"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environmental and Ecological Statistics","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"KhN1oPSLcE"}],"key":"N2KlOjLMqP"},{"type":"text","value":" 31,\n219-244, ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"UceuNzwtGc"},{"type":"cite","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10651-024-00615-9","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"child